tip: | Look at the car. | Two boxes on the grid: a long low one and a shorter one on top. The long side faces the light.
tip: 1 | Two boxes. | Block the body and the cabin first. The proportions decide whether it is a car, a van or a truck.
tip: 3 | Glass is a value, not a color. | The windows are a light cool ramp on the lit side and darker in front, with a slanted streak. They follow the same light as the paint.
tip: 4 | Wheels sit in arches. | A dark ring first and the wheel inside it, both skewed to lie on the side of the car. The wheels touch the tile, so the car stands on the grid.
